class:: OnsetStatistics2
summary:: Rolling onset interval statistics
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Rhythm
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/BeatTrack3

description::
A bounded timestamp ring retains rising-edge onsets from the trailing window. Rate is event count divided by the complete requested window; interval moments use only adjacent retained events.

This is an independent implementation of the statistical definition above. Output updates at the server control rate; beat boundaries are quantized to a control block. Silence produces zero level/density or missing tempo evidence. No corpus-level accuracy is implied.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: trig
Control-rate trigger. Only nonpositive-to-positive transitions count as events.

argument:: windowTime
Trailing history in seconds. Rhythm analysis accepts 0.5–16, default 6; onset/tempo statistics accept 0.05–60, default 4.

argument:: minGap
Minimum seconds between accepted events, default zero.

returns::
[eventsPerSecond, meanIntervalSeconds, intervalStandardDeviationSeconds, intervalCoefficientOfVariation]. Fewer than two events yields zero interval statistics.

examples::
OnsetStatistics2 measures rolling inter-onset intervals (IOI) from event triggers, returning event rate, mean interval, standard deviation, and coefficient of variation. In this example, mean IOI dynamically modulates the rate and pitch spread of an auxiliary generative bell cluster: fast drumming produces tight, high-pitched clusters, while sparse grooves produce slow, resonant chime strikes. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: tracks the mean IOI in seconds.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, 0.25);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, threshold: 0.15, fftSize: 1024, hop: 0.25);
        var stats = OnsetStatistics2.kr(onset[0], windowTime: 3.0);
        var meanIOI = stats[1].clip(0.05, 1.5).lag(0.05);

        // Algorithmic bell cluster triggered at rates derived from mean IOI
        var bellTrig = Impulse.kr((1.0 / meanIOI).clip(0.5, 10));
        var bellFreq = meanIOI.linexp(0.1, 1.0, 2200, 440);
        var bell = Ringz.ar(Decay2.ar(K2A.ar(bellTrig), 0.002, 0.05) * 0.05, bellFreq, 0.25) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + bell;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, stats[1]) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Mean IOI", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 1.0, "s");
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

